{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":27813,"name":"RikoKurnia","username":"RikoKurnia","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/rikokurnia/{size}/12402_2.png","created_at":"2026-11-24T22:03:43.605Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi everyone,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’ve been working on \u003cstrong\u003eOracell\u003c/strong\u003e, a contention-free oracle infrastructure built natively for Nervos CKB’s Cell Model as part of the CKB Builder Track (Week 11–12). Following initial architecture discussions, Phase 1 (MVP) is now live on \u003cstrong\u003ePudge Testnet\u003c/strong\u003e (\u003ccode\u003erikokurnia/oracell\u003c/code\u003e on GitHub, live app at \u003ccode\u003eoracell [dot] vercel [dot] app\u003c/code\u003e), and I’d love to gather technical feedback from the wider CKB community before moving into Phase 2.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27813-the-problem-were-solving-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27813-the-problem-were-solving-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eThe Problem We’re Solving\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTraditional push-based oracles map poorly onto CKB’s Extended UTXO (Cell) architecture:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCell Contention:\u003c/strong\u003e Updating a single shared price cell destroys its previous \u003ccode\u003eOutPoint\u003c/code\u003e, causing concurrent DeFi liquidations or swaps referencing that cell in the same block to fail.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCherry-Picking / Stale Quote Risks:\u003c/strong\u003e Because CKB-VM scripts execute deterministically without access to global block height or wall-clock time, loose signature windows allow latency arbitrage against older quotes.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCapacity Rent:\u003c/strong\u003e Requiring every consuming dApp to maintain and mutate its own on-chain price cell increases state rent and cycle overhead.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27813-phase-1-architecture-whats-live-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27813-phase-1-architecture-whats-live-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003ePhase 1 Architecture \u0026amp; What’s Live\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInstead of mutating a shared oracle cell, Oracell delivers signed multi-source market quotes (aggregated from CEX feeds with CKB anchor metadata) directly through the transaction \u003cstrong\u003ewitness\u003c/strong\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStateless Witness Verification:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ccode\u003e@oracell/sdk\u003c/code\u003e packs a \u003ccode\u003e184\u003c/code\u003e-byte BIP-340 Schnorr proof into \u003ccode\u003eWitnessArgs.output_type\u003c/code\u003e without consuming any shared oracle cell—allowing parallel transactions in the same block with zero contention.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTip-Header Binding (\u003ccode\u003eheader_deps\u003c/code\u003e):\u003c/strong\u003e Each quote commits to a recent CKB block hash. The on-chain RISC-V verifier (\u003ccode\u003eoracell-verifier\u003c/code\u003e) enforces a two-block freshness window relative to supplied \u003ccode\u003eheader_deps\u003c/code\u003e, while the SDK proof runner checks the live RPC tip at submission.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHosted API \u0026amp; SDK:\u003c/strong\u003e Both ESM and CommonJS clients of \u003ccode\u003e@oracell/sdk\u003c/code\u003e work out of the box against our hosted \u003ccode\u003e/api/oracle/feeds\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003e/api/oracle/quote\u003c/code\u003e endpoints without requiring a local server.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27813-verified-pudge-proof-benchmarks-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27813-verified-pudge-proof-benchmarks-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVerified Pudge Proof \u0026amp; Benchmarks\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCode Cell Deployment (Pudge):\u003c/strong\u003e Tx \u003ccode\u003e0xb2834f4487155d69fa5780a40819196cca1f818a3e62175bb9f2f39a7aeac0b1\u003c/code\u003e (Block \u003ccode\u003e23,135,440\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003e102,616\u003c/code\u003e bytes RISC-V ELF, \u003ccode\u003edata2\u003c/code\u003e)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eConfirmed Consuming Transaction:\u003c/strong\u003e Tx \u003ccode\u003e0x14beb0d8c0bc0b2a2f1c4aa788c3171284b4c5443074a28059e234cc5bf0ee90\u003c/code\u003e (Block \u003ccode\u003e23,135,450\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003e5,530,230\u003c/code\u003e RPC cycles)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCKB-VM Emulator Contention Benchmark:\u003c/strong\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eShared-cell baseline: \u003ccode\u003e1 / 20\u003c/code\u003e transactions admitted (\u003ccode\u003e19\u003c/code\u003e cell contention conflicts)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOracell stateless witness: \u003ccode\u003e100 / 100\u003c/code\u003e transactions verified (\u003ccode\u003e0\u003c/code\u003e conflicts, \u003ccode\u003e3,886,926\u003c/code\u003e cycles per verification)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eReferences (plain text while my new account’s link limit is still active):\u003c/strong\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGitHub Repository:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ccode\u003erikokurnia/oracell\u003c/code\u003e (commit \u003ccode\u003efb9f0b5\u003c/code\u003e, see \u003ccode\u003econtracts/DEPLOYMENT.md\u003c/code\u003e)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLive Explorer \u0026amp; Sandbox:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ccode\u003eoracell [dot] vercel [dot] app\u003c/code\u003e (\u003ccode\u003e/markets\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003e/docs\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003e/sandbox\u003c/code\u003e)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCKBuilder Technical Review Issue:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ccode\u003eNervos-Community-Catalyst/CKBuilder-projects\u003c/code\u003e Issue \u003ccode\u003e#57\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27813-explicit-phase-1-boundaries-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27813-explicit-phase-1-boundaries-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExplicit Phase 1 Boundaries\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo be completely transparent about current limitations:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSingle Publisher Key:\u003c/strong\u003e Phase 1 uses a single pinned BIP-340 Schnorr publisher key. Distributed key generation (DKG), threshold Schnorr aggregation (\u003ccode\u003eMuSig2\u003c/code\u003e / \u003ccode\u003eFROST\u003c/code\u003e), and CKB collateral staking/slashing are scoped for \u003cstrong\u003ePhase 3\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRelative \u003ccode\u003eheader_deps\u003c/code\u003e Freshness:\u003c/strong\u003e Because CKB-VM cannot read global state or the live network tip, the on-chain two-block window is evaluated relative to the transaction’s supplied \u003ccode\u003eheader_deps\u003c/code\u003e. In production DeFi/L2 flows, this is paired with client/co-signer tip verification at submission time.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27813-looking-for-community-feedback-next-phases-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27813-looking-for-community-feedback-next-phases-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eLooking for Community Feedback (Next Phases)\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBefore scoping a follow-up milestone (Phase 2), I would appreciate feedback from CKB developers on three questions:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCellScript Integration:\u003c/strong\u003e Would a native \u003cstrong\u003eCellScript\u003c/strong\u003e helper/module for consuming Oracell’s \u003ccode\u003e184\u003c/code\u003e-byte witness proof be useful for teams building CKB-Native DeFi protocols?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFiber Network \u0026amp; Perun Use Cases:\u003c/strong\u003e For builders working on \u003cstrong\u003eFiber\u003c/strong\u003e or \u003cstrong\u003ePerun\u003c/strong\u003e, is there active demand for discrete Schnorr nonces / DLC adaptor attestations for conditional swaps, hedging, or dispute resolution?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTestnet Early Adopters:\u003c/strong\u003e Are any teams building on Pudge interested in testing \u003ccode\u003e@oracell/sdk\u003c/code\u003e in a live dApp (lending, DEX, or hedging) and sharing integration friction points?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks in advance for taking a look—any critique on the verifier design, witness format, or roadmap priorities is very welcome.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-11-24T22:03:43.605Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":5,"reads":27,"readers_count":26,"score":105.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":11368,"topic_slug":"oracell-contention-free-witness-oracle-for-nervos-ckb-phase-1-mvp-live-on-pudge-feedback-welcome","display_username":"RikoKurnia","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":3}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":4573,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/oracell-contention-free-witness-oracle-for-nervos-ckb-phase-1-mvp-live-on-pudge-feedback-welcome/11368/1","babel_translations_meta":[{"language":"es","status":"completed","source_language":"en"},{"language":"zh-cn","status":"completed","source_language":"en"}],"show_translation_widget":true,"show_translation_button":true,"babel_detected_locale":"en","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":3}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":3,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false,"can_translate":false},{"id":27831,"name":"Ayoub Lesfer","username":"Ayoub_Lesfer","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/ayoub_lesfer/{size}/10917_2.png","created_at":"2026-11-25T16:45:12.474Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eRan into the same wall on CrowdCell from the other side. since only gives you a lower bound, so a script can say “not before block X” but never “not after”, which is why pledges after a campaign’s deadline are still possible on our testnet until someone finalizes. A header_dep near the deadline narrows it but anyone can pick an older header. I think your window has the same shape: the two blocks are counted from whatever header the tx brings, so a quote stays valid on chain if you submit it later with its own header. Is the co-signer going to be required on chain in Phase 2, or is the SDK tip check the only guard? Feels like that’s where the freshness actually lives.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-11-25T16:45:12.474Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":18,"readers_count":17,"score":38.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":11368,"topic_slug":"oracell-contention-free-witness-oracle-for-nervos-ckb-phase-1-mvp-live-on-pudge-feedback-welcome","display_username":"Ayoub Lesfer","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":2}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":4224,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/oracell-contention-free-witness-oracle-for-nervos-ckb-phase-1-mvp-live-on-pudge-feedback-welcome/11368/2","babel_translations_meta":[{"language":"es","status":"completed","source_language":"en"},{"language":"zh-cn","status":"completed","source_language":"en"}],"show_translation_widget":true,"show_translation_button":true,"babel_detected_locale":"en","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":2}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":2,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_translate":false},{"id":27839,"name":"RikoKurnia","username":"RikoKurnia","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/rikokurnia/{size}/12402_2.png","created_at":"2026-11-26T02:30:53.223Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eGreat point \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/ayoub_lesfer\"\u003e@Ayoub_Lesfer\u003c/a\u003e — you nailed where the freshness boundary lives. The SDK tip check is just a Phase 1 client guard; it can’t stop someone from submitting an old quote with its matching \u003ccode\u003eheader_dep\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn Phase 2, we plan to require a counterparty/keeper co-signature on-chain for L1 DeFi (who verifies the live tip before signing), while in L2 channels (Fiber/Perun) freshness is checked off-chain before both peers sign.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDid you end up using a keeper/finalizer to close campaigns after the deadline on CrowdCell?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-11-26T02:35:01.221Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":2,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":16,"readers_count":15,"score":23.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":11368,"topic_slug":"oracell-contention-free-witness-oracle-for-nervos-ckb-phase-1-mvp-live-on-pudge-feedback-welcome","display_username":"RikoKurnia","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":3,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":4224,"username":"Ayoub_Lesfer","name":"Ayoub Lesfer","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/ayoub_lesfer/{size}/10917_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":4573,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/oracell-contention-free-witness-oracle-for-nervos-ckb-phase-1-mvp-live-on-pudge-feedback-welcome/11368/3","babel_translations_meta":[{"language":"es","status":"completed","source_language":"en"},{"language":"zh-cn","status":"completed","source_language":"en"}],"show_translation_widget":true,"show_translation_button":true,"babel_detected_locale":"en","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_translate":false},{"id":27904,"name":"Ayoub Lesfer","username":"Ayoub_Lesfer","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/ayoub_lesfer/{size}/10917_2.png","created_at":"2026-11-27T16:31:41.233Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eYeah, once the deadline passes anyone can finalize, the campaign lock only checks that the tx’s since is past the deadline block. We run a keeper that finalizes expired campaigns and then releases or refunds the pledges every cycle, and it’s split out so anyone can run their own, psawyerberlin already runs a second one on his node. The gap you’d expect is still there though, a pledge can land between the deadline and the finalize tx, so closing that window is on our list. Makes sense to put the co-signer on chain for L1, otherwise the SDK check is just a suggestion.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-11-27T16:31:41.233Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":3,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":14,"readers_count":13,"score":2.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":11368,"topic_slug":"oracell-contention-free-witness-oracle-for-nervos-ckb-phase-1-mvp-live-on-pudge-feedback-welcome","display_username":"Ayoub Lesfer","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":4573,"username":"RikoKurnia","name":"RikoKurnia","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/rikokurnia/{size}/12402_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":4224,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/oracell-contention-free-witness-oracle-for-nervos-ckb-phase-1-mvp-live-on-pudge-feedback-welcome/11368/4","babel_translations_meta":[{"language":"es","status":"completed","source_language":"en"},{"language":"zh-cn","status":"completed","source_language":"en"}],"show_translation_widget":true,"show_translation_button":true,"babel_detected_locale":"en","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepte